{"post_stream":{"posts":[{"id":114060,"name":"","username":"sanghoon_lee","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discourse.openrobotics.org/sanghoon_lee/{size}/24914_2.png","created_at":"2026-06-12T01:58:06.974Z","cooked":"\u003cblockquote\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eros2probe is a drop-in replacement for \u003ccode\u003erosbag2\u003c/code\u003e and \u003ccode\u003eros2 topic\u003c/code\u003e that does not perturb the system it observes.\u003c/strong\u003e It records and monitors ROS 2 traffic from outside the DDS domain. No extra subscriber, no observer-induced drops, far less CPU and memory. It reports exactly the loss the real subscriber saw, and the CLI mirrors ROS 2, so you just swap \u003ccode\u003eros2\u003c/code\u003e for \u003ccode\u003erp\u003c/code\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://github.com/csi-dgist/ros2probe\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003eCode\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/strong\u003e · \u003cstrong\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.10746\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003ePaper (arXiv)\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/strong\u003e · \u003cstrong\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://csi-dgist.github.io/ros2probe-page/\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003eProject page\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"lightbox-wrapper\"\u003e\u003ca class=\"lightbox\" href=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/flex022/uploads/ros/original/3X/7/c/7ca5bf1bc252eafb3a24db03c8f75099965d85c1.jpeg\" data-download-href=\"/uploads/short-url/hMGjD3kNfjVsApsG09MfJtWs7fz.jpeg?dl=1\" title=\"concept architecture\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003e\u003cimg src=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/flex022/uploads/ros/optimized/3X/7/c/7ca5bf1bc252eafb3a24db03c8f75099965d85c1_2_690x396.jpeg\" alt=\"concept architecture\" data-base62-sha1=\"hMGjD3kNfjVsApsG09MfJtWs7fz\" width=\"690\" height=\"396\" srcset=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/flex022/uploads/ros/optimized/3X/7/c/7ca5bf1bc252eafb3a24db03c8f75099965d85c1_2_690x396.jpeg, https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/flex022/uploads/ros/optimized/3X/7/c/7ca5bf1bc252eafb3a24db03c8f75099965d85c1_2_1035x594.jpeg 1.5x, https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/flex022/uploads/ros/original/3X/7/c/7ca5bf1bc252eafb3a24db03c8f75099965d85c1.jpeg 2x\" data-dominant-color=\"E2E5EA\"\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"meta\"\u003e\u003csvg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-far-image svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cuse href=\"#far-image\"\u003e\u003c/use\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003cspan class=\"filename\"\u003econcept architecture\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"informations\"\u003e1280×736 102 KB\u003c/span\u003e\u003csvg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-discourse-expand svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cuse href=\"#discourse-expand\"\u003e\u003c/use\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-114060-why-this-exists-1\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-114060-why-this-exists-1\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eWhy this exists\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eEvery standard observer (\u003ccode\u003erosbag2\u003c/code\u003e, \u003ccode\u003eros2 topic echo\u003c/code\u003e / \u003ccode\u003ehz\u003c/code\u003e, the \u003ccode\u003eros2 daemon\u003c/code\u003e,\u003cbr\u003e\nDDS vendor monitors) sees your data by subscribing. That adds a DataReader, the\u003cbr\u003e\npublisher sends an extra copy, and near link saturation that copy steals\u003cbr\u003e\nbandwidth from the real subscriber. The observer also reads a different copy, so\u003cbr\u003e\nthe loss it reports is not the loss your subscriber actually experienced. This\u003cbr\u003e\nis structural to DDS pub/sub, not a bug in any one tool.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-114060-what-ros2probe-does-differently-2\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-114060-what-ros2probe-does-differently-2\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eWhat ros2probe does differently\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003ePassive eBPF wire tap.\u003c/strong\u003e Reads a kernel copy of RTPS off the wire.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eNever joins the domain.\u003c/strong\u003e No participant, no DataReader, nothing added to the wire.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eReads the same packets the subscriber gets.\u003c/strong\u003e The loss and latency it reports match what the subscriber actually saw (recall 1.0).\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eFull reconstruction in userspace.\u003c/strong\u003e Topic graph, per-topic metrics, and message streams, independent of the DDS vendor.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-114060-results-on-real-hardware-3\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-114060-results-on-real-hardware-3\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eResults on real hardware\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e3 platforms (laptop, Jetson, Raspberry Pi), 2 DDS implementations (Fast DDS, Cyclone DDS), 7 workloads, wired and wireless, two QoS settings.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"md-table\"\u003e\n\u003ctable\u003e\n\u003cthead\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\n\u003cth\u003e\u003c/th\u003e\n\u003cth\u003eros2probe\u003c/th\u003e\n\u003cth\u003eexisting ros2 tools\u003c/th\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003c/thead\u003e\n\u003ctbody\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003eLoss it causes on the subscriber (recording the full near-GbE workload)\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e0%\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003eup to \u003cstrong\u003e75.5%\u003c/strong\u003e (rosbag2)\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003eLoss it reports vs what the subscriber saw\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eexact, recall 1.0\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e0.09 (rosbag2 at 10% loss)\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003eDiscovery graph perturbation\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e\u003cstrong\u003ewithin 0.5%\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003eup to \u003cstrong\u003e2.6x inflation\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003eObserver CPU\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eup to 7x lower\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003ebaseline\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003eObserver memory\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eup to 28x lower\u003c/strong\u003e (1.7 MB vs ~47 MB)\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003ebaseline\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003c/tbody\u003e\n\u003c/table\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"lightbox-wrapper\"\u003e\u003ca class=\"lightbox\" href=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/flex022/uploads/ros/original/3X/f/f/ff0b27a4219e8176bace814b6d6edc05ce784626.jpeg\" data-download-href=\"/uploads/short-url/AodEyqhQWClH2b6tDCmo0ZwsTAi.jpeg?dl=1\" title=\"exp2_results\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003e\u003cimg src=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/flex022/uploads/ros/optimized/3X/f/f/ff0b27a4219e8176bace814b6d6edc05ce784626_2_670x500.jpeg\" alt=\"exp2_results\" data-base62-sha1=\"AodEyqhQWClH2b6tDCmo0ZwsTAi\" width=\"670\" height=\"500\" srcset=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/flex022/uploads/ros/optimized/3X/f/f/ff0b27a4219e8176bace814b6d6edc05ce784626_2_670x500.jpeg, https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/flex022/uploads/ros/optimized/3X/f/f/ff0b27a4219e8176bace814b6d6edc05ce784626_2_1005x750.jpeg 1.5x, https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/flex022/uploads/ros/optimized/3X/f/f/ff0b27a4219e8176bace814b6d6edc05ce784626_2_1340x1000.jpeg 2x\" data-dominant-color=\"F4F4F5\"\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"meta\"\u003e\u003csvg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-far-image svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cuse href=\"#far-image\"\u003e\u003c/use\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003cspan class=\"filename\"\u003eexp2_results\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"informations\"\u003e1920×1431 227 KB\u003c/span\u003e\u003csvg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-discourse-expand svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cuse href=\"#discourse-expand\"\u003e\u003c/use\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOn a Raspberry Pi 4B, \u003ccode\u003eros2 topic hz\u003c/code\u003e saturates a CPU core while ros2probe stays under 30%.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-114060-usage-you-already-know-the-commands-4\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-114060-usage-you-already-know-the-commands-4\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eUsage. You already know the commands\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eInstall once, then replace \u003ccode\u003eros2\u003c/code\u003e with \u003ccode\u003erp\u003c/code\u003e:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cpre\u003e\u003ccode class=\"lang-auto\"\u003eros2 topic hz   /scan    -\u0026gt;    rp topic hz   /scan\nros2 bag record /scan    -\u0026gt;    rp bag record /scan\n\n\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eRecordings are written as MCAP and replay with \u003ccode\u003eros2 bag play\u003c/code\u003e. Scripts and CI\u003cbr\u003e\nthat parse \u003ccode\u003ehz\u003c/code\u003e output keep working unchanged.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eros2probe also ships a GUI (\u003ccode\u003erp gui\u003c/code\u003e) with a live ROS graph, a per-topic monitor, and an MCAP recorder.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"lightbox-wrapper\"\u003e\u003ca class=\"lightbox\" href=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/flex022/uploads/ros/original/3X/6/e/6e56feac46607d5e07acc7623e07023cfa657a49.png\" data-download-href=\"/uploads/short-url/fK6UfB46dYSCTigZAvmDyRr5j8B.png?dl=1\" title=\"dashboard\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003e\u003cimg src=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/flex022/uploads/ros/optimized/3X/6/e/6e56feac46607d5e07acc7623e07023cfa657a49_2_690x393.png\" alt=\"dashboard\" data-base62-sha1=\"fK6UfB46dYSCTigZAvmDyRr5j8B\" width=\"690\" height=\"393\" srcset=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/flex022/uploads/ros/optimized/3X/6/e/6e56feac46607d5e07acc7623e07023cfa657a49_2_690x393.png, https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/flex022/uploads/ros/optimized/3X/6/e/6e56feac46607d5e07acc7623e07023cfa657a49_2_1035x589.png 1.5x, https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/flex022/uploads/ros/optimized/3X/6/e/6e56feac46607d5e07acc7623e07023cfa657a49_2_1380x786.png 2x\" data-dominant-color=\"E4E7EA\"\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"meta\"\u003e\u003csvg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-far-image svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cuse href=\"#far-image\"\u003e\u003c/use\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003cspan class=\"filename\"\u003edashboard\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"informations\"\u003e1849×1054 184 KB\u003c/span\u003e\u003csvg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-discourse-expand svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cuse href=\"#discourse-expand\"\u003e\u003c/use\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"lightbox-wrapper\"\u003e\u003ca class=\"lightbox\" href=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/flex022/uploads/ros/original/3X/0/8/0851b0a94da7381f0d0951d356b875606b72e300.jpeg\" data-download-href=\"/uploads/short-url/1bAQ4NZphBPIN2JrMYwjLBhqrny.jpeg?dl=1\" title=\"topic-monitor2\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003e\u003cimg src=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/flex022/uploads/ros/optimized/3X/0/8/0851b0a94da7381f0d0951d356b875606b72e300_2_690x392.jpeg\" alt=\"topic-monitor2\" data-base62-sha1=\"1bAQ4NZphBPIN2JrMYwjLBhqrny\" width=\"690\" height=\"392\" srcset=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/flex022/uploads/ros/optimized/3X/0/8/0851b0a94da7381f0d0951d356b875606b72e300_2_690x392.jpeg, https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/flex022/uploads/ros/optimized/3X/0/8/0851b0a94da7381f0d0951d356b875606b72e300_2_1035x588.jpeg 1.5x, https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/flex022/uploads/ros/optimized/3X/0/8/0851b0a94da7381f0d0951d356b875606b72e300_2_1380x784.jpeg 2x\" data-dominant-color=\"E3E5E9\"\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"meta\"\u003e\u003csvg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-far-image svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cuse href=\"#far-image\"\u003e\u003c/use\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003cspan class=\"filename\"\u003etopic-monitor2\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"informations\"\u003e1851×1053 182 KB\u003c/span\u003e\u003csvg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-discourse-expand svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cuse href=\"#discourse-expand\"\u003e\u003c/use\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"lightbox-wrapper\"\u003e\u003ca class=\"lightbox\" href=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/flex022/uploads/ros/original/3X/6/d/6d3e48e01b3c006ad2b901237f7d63b28b6c2274.jpeg\" data-download-href=\"/uploads/short-url/fApui3sxyWIl6AAS6TroWMHn6wA.jpeg?dl=1\" title=\"bag-recorder1\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003e\u003cimg src=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/flex022/uploads/ros/optimized/3X/6/d/6d3e48e01b3c006ad2b901237f7d63b28b6c2274_2_690x393.jpeg\" alt=\"bag-recorder1\" data-base62-sha1=\"fApui3sxyWIl6AAS6TroWMHn6wA\" width=\"690\" height=\"393\" srcset=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/flex022/uploads/ros/optimized/3X/6/d/6d3e48e01b3c006ad2b901237f7d63b28b6c2274_2_690x393.jpeg, https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/flex022/uploads/ros/optimized/3X/6/d/6d3e48e01b3c006ad2b901237f7d63b28b6c2274_2_1035x589.jpeg 1.5x, https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/flex022/uploads/ros/optimized/3X/6/d/6d3e48e01b3c006ad2b901237f7d63b28b6c2274_2_1380x786.jpeg 2x\" data-dominant-color=\"DADBDF\"\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"meta\"\u003e\u003csvg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-far-image svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cuse href=\"#far-image\"\u003e\u003c/use\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003cspan class=\"filename\"\u003ebag-recorder1\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"informations\"\u003e1850×1054 111 KB\u003c/span\u003e\u003csvg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-discourse-expand svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cuse href=\"#discourse-expand\"\u003e\u003c/use\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-114060-status-5\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-114060-status-5\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eStatus\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eWorks today on RTPS-based DDS. Tested on Fast DDS and Cyclone DDS.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eShared-memory (SHM) transport is a structural limit, not a blind spot. The\u003cbr\u003e\ntopic graph is still recovered passively from discovery on the network, but\u003cbr\u003e\nSHM payloads never reach the wire, so observing them falls back to a\u003cbr\u003e\nshort-lived, namespace-isolated shadow subscriber that joins the domain. For\u003cbr\u003e\nthose topics ros2probe still works, but gives up its probe-effect-free\u003cbr\u003e\nguarantee. Network-transported topics keep the full benefit.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eZenoh (rmw_zenoh) uses a different wire protocol and is planned. RViz\u003cbr\u003e\nintegration is on the roadmap.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-114060-links-6\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-114060-links-6\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eLinks\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eProject page (more figures and experiment plots): \u003ca href=\"https://csi-dgist.github.io/ros2probe-page/\" class=\"inline-onebox\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003eros2probe · Non-intrusive Observability for ROS 2\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eCode: \u003ca href=\"https://github.com/csi-dgist/ros2probe\" class=\"inline-onebox\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003eGitHub - csi-dgist/ros2probe: Host-level observability for ROS 2 middleware traffic, without creating any ROS 2 subscriptions. · GitHub\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003ePaper (arXiv): \u003ca href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.10746\" class=\"inline-onebox\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003e[2606.10746] ros2probe: Non-intrusive, Kernel-selective Observability for Robot Operating System 2 Middleware\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/sanghoon-lee-ros-ai_ros2-dds-middleware-activity-7470852642492227585-gxBc\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003eBackground writeup on LinkedIn\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFeedback, issues, and real use cases are very welcome.\u003cbr\u003e\nIf you are curious about my other work, see \u003ca href=\"https://hun0130.github.io/\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003ehttps://hun0130.github.io/\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":1,"post_type":1,"posts_count":8,"updated_at":"2026-06-12T02:06:56.814Z","reply_count":1,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":184,"reads":86,"readers_count":85,"score":1152.0,"yours":false,"topic_id":55430,"topic_slug":"ros2probe-observe-ros-2-traffic-without-the-probe-effect-swap-ros2-rp","display_username":"","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":2,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"link_counts":[{"url":"https://github.com/csi-dgist/ros2probe","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"GitHub - csi-dgist/ros2probe: Host-level observability for ROS 2 middleware traffic, without creating any ROS 2 subscriptions. · GitHub","clicks":36},{"url":"https://csi-dgist.github.io/ros2probe-page/","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"ros2probe · Non-intrusive Observability for ROS 2","clicks":28},{"url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.10746","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"[2606.10746] ros2probe: Non-intrusive, Kernel-selective Observability for Robot Operating System 2 Middleware","clicks":3},{"url":"https://hun0130.github.io/","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"Sanghoon Lee — Cyber-Physical AI Researcher · DGIST","clicks":3},{"url":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/sanghoon-lee-ros-ai_ros2-dds-middleware-activity-7470852642492227585-gxBc","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"#ros2 #dds #middleware #fastdds #cyclonedds #robotics #embeddedsystems #observability #robotsoftware #slam #teleoperation #autonomousvehicles #ebpf #linux #robotengineering #mobilerobots #opensource | Sanghoon Lee","clicks":0},{"url":"https://discourse.openrobotics.org/t/ros-news-for-the-week-of-june-8th-2026/55449","internal":true,"reflection":true,"title":"ROS News for the Week of June 8th, 2026","clicks":1},{"url":"https://discourse.openrobotics.org/t/ros-news-for-the-week-of-june-22nd-2026/55738","internal":true,"reflection":true,"title":"ROS News for the Week of June 22nd, 2026","clicks":0}],"read":true,"user_title":"","bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[{"id":2,"count":12}],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":30901,"hidden":false,"trust_level":1,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":true,"wiki":false,"mentioned_users":[],"post_url":"/t/ros2probe-observe-ros-2-traffic-without-the-probe-effect-swap-ros2-rp/55430/1","reactions":[{"id":"heart","type":"emoji","count":11},{"id":"open_mouth","type":"emoji","count":1}],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":12,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_vote":false},{"id":114061,"name":"Christian Fritz","username":"chfritz","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discourse.openrobotics.org/chfritz/{size}/26180_2.png","created_at":"2026-06-12T02:17:47.054Z","cooked":"\u003caside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"sanghoon_lee\" data-post=\"1\" data-topic=\"55430\"\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"title\"\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"quote-controls\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cimg alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://sea2.discourse-cdn.com/flex022/user_avatar/discourse.openrobotics.org/sanghoon_lee/48/24914_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"\u003e sanghoon_lee:\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cblockquote\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003ePassive eBPF wire tap\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\n\u003c/aside\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThat’s such a great idea!\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFYI, \u003ca class=\"mention\" href=\"/u/pablothepenguin\"\u003e@pablothepenguin\u003c/a\u003e , seems relevant to your \u003ccode\u003eros_tap\u003c/code\u003e tool.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":2,"post_type":1,"posts_count":8,"updated_at":"2026-06-12T02:19:51.662Z","reply_count":1,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":1,"incoming_link_count":4,"reads":75,"readers_count":74,"score":39.8,"yours":false,"topic_id":55430,"topic_slug":"ros2probe-observe-ros-2-traffic-without-the-probe-effect-swap-ros2-rp","display_username":"Christian Fritz","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":"Regular","title_is_group":false,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":19122,"hidden":false,"trust_level":3,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":true,"wiki":false,"mentioned_users":[{"id":36067,"username":"pablothepenguin","name":"Pablo","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discourse.openrobotics.org/pablothepenguin/{size}/34223_2.png"}],"post_url":"/t/ros2probe-observe-ros-2-traffic-without-the-probe-effect-swap-ros2-rp/55430/2","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false},{"id":114073,"name":"Michał Fąferek","username":"Michal_Faferek","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discourse.openrobotics.org/michal_faferek/{size}/31614_2.png","created_at":"2026-06-12T10:55:39.336Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003enice work, the shadow subscriber trick is really clever!\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e1 thing worth fixing though: the README says the filter attaches to non-loopback interfaces only and that SHM-only topics are excluded from recording, but from what I see the code always captures on \u003ccode\u003elo\u003c/code\u003e and spawns the shadow sub for SHM topics, so single-host actually works better than the README suggests, right? \u003cimg src=\"https://emoji.discourse-cdn.com/noto/smiley.png?v=15\" title=\":smiley:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":smiley:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI’d like to try the passive hz/delay metrics as an input for health monitoring in \u003ca href=\"https://github.com/selfpatch/ros2_medkit\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003eros2_medkit\u003c/a\u003e, where single-host is the common case\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003ca class=\"mention\" href=\"/u/sanghoon_lee\"\u003e@sanghoon_lee\u003c/a\u003e I will report back once we’ve given it a proper test \u003cimg src=\"https://emoji.discourse-cdn.com/noto/sweat_smile.png?v=15\" title=\":sweat_smile:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":sweat_smile:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"\u003e\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":3,"post_type":1,"posts_count":8,"updated_at":"2026-06-12T10:55:39.336Z","reply_count":1,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":8,"reads":68,"readers_count":67,"score":58.4,"yours":false,"topic_id":55430,"topic_slug":"ros2probe-observe-ros-2-traffic-without-the-probe-effect-swap-ros2-rp","display_username":"Michał Fąferek","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"link_counts":[{"url":"https://github.com/selfpatch/ros2_medkit","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"GitHub - selfpatch/ros2_medkit: ros2_medkit - diagnostics gateway for ROS 2 robots. Faults, live data, operations, scripts, locking, triggers, and OTA updates via REST API. No SSH, no custom tooling. · GitHub","clicks":5}],"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":34100,"hidden":false,"trust_level":1,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":true,"wiki":false,"mentioned_users":[{"id":30901,"username":"sanghoon_lee","name":"","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discourse.openrobotics.org/sanghoon_lee/{size}/24914_2.png"}],"post_url":"/t/ros2probe-observe-ros-2-traffic-without-the-probe-effect-swap-ros2-rp/55430/3","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false},{"id":114134,"name":"","username":"sanghoon_lee","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discourse.openrobotics.org/sanghoon_lee/{size}/24914_2.png","created_at":"2026-06-15T01:30:21.616Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eThanks for the kind words, and great catch on the README. You’re right, the code does capture on \u003ccode\u003elo\u003c/code\u003e and spawns the shadow sub for SHM topics, so single-host works better than the docs claim. I’ll fix it to match the actual behavior.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe \u003ccode\u003eros2_medkit\u003c/code\u003e idea sounds really interesting. Using the passive hz/delay metrics as a health-monitoring input is exactly the kind of use case I was hoping people would find. Please do give it a spin and let me know how it goes, and feel free to throw any rough edges or feature requests my way. Looking forward to your report!\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":4,"post_type":1,"posts_count":8,"updated_at":"2026-06-15T01:31:59.284Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":3,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":1,"reads":55,"readers_count":54,"score":31.0,"yours":false,"topic_id":55430,"topic_slug":"ros2probe-observe-ros-2-traffic-without-the-probe-effect-swap-ros2-rp","display_username":"","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":3,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":"","reply_to_user":{"id":34100,"username":"Michal_Faferek","name":"Michał Fąferek","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discourse.openrobotics.org/michal_faferek/{size}/31614_2.png"},"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[{"id":2,"count":1}],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":30901,"hidden":false,"trust_level":1,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":true,"wiki":false,"mentioned_users":[],"post_url":"/t/ros2probe-observe-ros-2-traffic-without-the-probe-effect-swap-ros2-rp/55430/4","reactions":[{"id":"+1","type":"emoji","count":1}],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":1,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false},{"id":114135,"name":"","username":"sanghoon_lee","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discourse.openrobotics.org/sanghoon_lee/{size}/24914_2.png","created_at":"2026-06-15T01:31:36.176Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eThanks, that means a lot! And thanks for the pointer to \u003ccode\u003eros_tap\u003c/code\u003e. I went and read through it, and I think they’re actually after fairly different things.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFrom what I can tell, \u003ccode\u003eros_tap\u003c/code\u003e joins the DDS network as a CycloneDDS participant and subscribes to stream telemetry (JSONL to stdout, disk, or S3), which is a clean fit for zero-config fleet capture from any machine. ros2probe goes the opposite direction and sits below the middleware, reading a kernel copy of the RTPS packets via eBPF, so it never joins the graph at all. That no-participant part is really the whole point for us, since adding a subscriber is exactly the probe effect we’re trying to avoid.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSo different layer and different goal, but I appreciate the connection.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":5,"post_type":1,"posts_count":8,"updated_at":"2026-06-15T01:31:36.176Z","reply_count":1,"reply_to_post_number":2,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":57,"readers_count":56,"score":16.4,"yours":false,"topic_id":55430,"topic_slug":"ros2probe-observe-ros-2-traffic-without-the-probe-effect-swap-ros2-rp","display_username":"","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":"","reply_to_user":{"id":19122,"username":"chfritz","name":"Christian Fritz","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discourse.openrobotics.org/chfritz/{size}/26180_2.png"},"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":30901,"hidden":false,"trust_level":1,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":true,"wiki":false,"mentioned_users":[],"post_url":"/t/ros2probe-observe-ros-2-traffic-without-the-probe-effect-swap-ros2-rp/55430/5","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false},{"id":114136,"name":"Christian Fritz","username":"chfritz","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discourse.openrobotics.org/chfritz/{size}/26180_2.png","created_at":"2026-06-15T04:26:19.046Z","cooked":"\u003caside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"sanghoon_lee\" data-post=\"5\" data-topic=\"55430\"\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"title\"\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"quote-controls\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cimg alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://sea2.discourse-cdn.com/flex022/user_avatar/discourse.openrobotics.org/sanghoon_lee/48/24914_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"\u003e sanghoon_lee:\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cblockquote\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThat no-participant part is really the whole point for us, since adding a subscriber is exactly the probe effect we’re trying to avoid.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\n\u003c/aside\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eYes, I know. And I think that’s the better approach for the recording \u003ccode\u003eros_tap\u003c/code\u003e aims to do as well, so thought I Pablo might be interested.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":6,"post_type":1,"posts_count":8,"updated_at":"2026-06-15T04:26:19.046Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":5,"quote_count":1,"incoming_link_count":2,"reads":54,"readers_count":53,"score":20.8,"yours":false,"topic_id":55430,"topic_slug":"ros2probe-observe-ros-2-traffic-without-the-probe-effect-swap-ros2-rp","display_username":"Christian Fritz","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":"Regular","title_is_group":false,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":19122,"hidden":false,"trust_level":3,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":true,"wiki":false,"mentioned_users":[],"post_url":"/t/ros2probe-observe-ros-2-traffic-without-the-probe-effect-swap-ros2-rp/55430/6","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false},{"id":114295,"name":"zc Liu","username":"zc_Liu","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discourse.openrobotics.org/zc_liu/{size}/31617_2.png","created_at":"2026-06-20T05:13:47.268Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eThis is excellent work. The “observer effect” problem in ROS 2 tooling is very real, especially near bandwidth or CPU saturation. A non-intrusive RTPS/eBPF-level recorder is a very valuable layer.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOne thought: this seems highly complementary to a different class of runtime assurance tools that operate above transport-level observability.\u003ccode\u003eros2probe\u003c/code\u003e answers questions like:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cpre\u003e\u003ccode class=\"lang-auto\"\u003eDid the real subscriber receive the packet?\nWas there DDS/RTPS loss?\nDid the observer perturb the graph or add load?\nWhat latency/loss did the subscriber actually see?\n\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThere is another failure plane where the transport can be perfectly healthy, but the \u003cstrong\u003econtrol intent is no longer semantically or physically healthy\u003c/strong\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor example, in PX4 Offboard autonomy, the network may deliver every \u003ccode\u003e/fmu/in/trajectory_setpoint\u003c/code\u003e packet correctly, but the upstream planner / VIO / perception stack may be delayed, bursty, or re-emitting setpoints that are stale relative to the current vehicle state. In that case, a transport-level probe can correctly report “delivery is fine,” while the autonomy stack still needs a boundary-level check:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cpre\u003e\u003ccode class=\"lang-auto\"\u003eIs the setpoint stream fresh?\nIs it jittered?\nIs it consistent with the current Offboard mode?\nIs the vehicle response physically matching the intent stream?\n\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI have been experimenting with this complementary layer in a small ROS 2 / PX4 project called AFIO, currently reframing it as \u003cstrong\u003eAutonomy Flight Integrity Observer\u003c/strong\u003e. It is a passive Offboard boundary observer that watches:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cpre\u003e\u003ccode class=\"lang-auto\"\u003e/fmu/in/trajectory_setpoint\n/fmu/in/offboard_control_mode\n/fmu/out/vehicle_odometry\n\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eand publishes standard \u003ccode\u003e/diagnostics\u003c/code\u003e plus CSV labels such as:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cpre\u003e\u003ccode class=\"lang-auto\"\u003esetpointAgeMs\nsetpointJitterMs\nstaleStreams\npositionTrackingResidual\nvelocityTrackingResidual\nflightResidual\ndominantCause\n\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIn controlled PX4/Gazebo latency-injection tests, the transport can remain syntactically valid while the Offboard boundary transitions from healthy → \u003ccode\u003eSETPOINT_JITTER\u003c/code\u003e → \u003ccode\u003eSTALE_STREAM\u003c/code\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI see a very natural integration path:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cpre\u003e\u003ccode class=\"lang-auto\"\u003eros2probe:\n  non-intrusive capture / MCAP / true subscriber-side transport metrics\n\nAFIO:\n  domain-level residual analysis on trajectory_setpoint + odometry + mode semantics\n\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThat combination could give both:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cpre\u003e\u003ccode class=\"lang-auto\"\u003eDid the subscriber receive the data?\nand\nWas the received data still a valid control intent for the vehicle?\n\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eQuestion: does \u003ccode\u003eros2probe\u003c/code\u003e expose reconstructed message payloads and timestamps in a way that downstream tools can consume live or from MCAP? If so, it would be very interesting to run Offboard boundary-integrity analysis on top of ros2probe recordings without adding any extra ROS 2 subscribers.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAFIO repo for reference: \u003ca href=\"https://github.com/ZC502/ai_flight_integrity_observer.git\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003ehttps://github.com/ZC502/ai_flight_integrity_observer.git\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":7,"post_type":1,"posts_count":8,"updated_at":"2026-06-20T05:13:47.268Z","reply_count":1,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":3,"reads":36,"readers_count":35,"score":27.2,"yours":false,"topic_id":55430,"topic_slug":"ros2probe-observe-ros-2-traffic-without-the-probe-effect-swap-ros2-rp","display_username":"zc Liu","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"link_count